1
00:00:00,174 --> 00:00:02,984
What if all one point four
billion Indians lived in Mumbai?

2
00:00:03,229 --> 00:00:06,699
Mumbai city covers only around
six hundred square kilometres.

3
00:00:06,950 --> 00:00:09,500
It's already one of the most
crowded cities on Earth.

4
00:00:09,565 --> 00:00:11,075
But put the whole country inside,

5
00:00:11,505 --> 00:00:14,335
and it would be over a hundred
times more crowded than today.

6
00:00:14,401 --> 00:00:16,571
Millions of people per square kilometre.

7
00:00:16,571 --> 00:00:19,101
There'd be no space for homes,
roads or parks.

8
00:00:19,302 --> 00:00:21,932
Local trains, already packed,
would be impossible.

9
00:00:22,152 --> 00:00:26,387
And the city would need an unimaginable
amount of water every single day.

10
00:00:26,387 --> 00:00:27,297
To fit everyone,

11
00:00:27,687 --> 00:00:30,097
Mumbai would have to grow
far outside its boundaries,

12
00:00:30,427 --> 00:00:32,557
swallowing neighbouring
cities and villages.

13
00:00:32,848 --> 00:00:34,278
Mumbai is already packed.

14
00:00:34,438 --> 00:00:36,608
So what if the whole of
India lived in Mumbai?

